From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] CLI: request scalar text from context-sensitive generators

The module intentionally returns a list in list context and a joined
string in scalar context. print supplies list context to its operands,
so the CLI printed generated words without separators. Request the
documented string form for each command-line mode.

---
 bin/lorem | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bin/lorem b/bin/lorem
--- a/bin/lorem
+++ b/bin/lorem
@@ -19,13 +19,13 @@ die usage()
 my $lorem = Text::Lorem->new;
 if ($opt_w) {
-    print $lorem->words($opt_w);
+    print scalar $lorem->words($opt_w);
 }
 elsif ($opt_s) {
-    print $lorem->sentences($opt_s);
+    print scalar $lorem->sentences($opt_s);
 }
 elsif ($opt_p) {
-    print $lorem->paragraphs($opt_p);
+    print scalar $lorem->paragraphs($opt_p);
 }
 else {
-    print $lorem->paragraphs(1);
+    print scalar $lorem->paragraphs(1);
 }
